From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:05:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the index lock's locked index as used outside its assertion

IndexLock keeps a reference to the index it locked only for AssertHeld()
to compare against, and reads it nowhere but inside D_ASSERT(). In a
release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, clang reports the
field under -Wunused-private-field. A (void) cast after the assertion
marks it used, the way the engine already treats locals that only an
assertion reads.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/execution/index/index_lock.hpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/execution/index/index_lock.hpp b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/execution/index/index_lock.hpp
index 7e13483a07..5e13b4fc29 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/execution/index/index_lock.hpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/execution/index/index_lock.hpp
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ public:
 	//! Verify that a borrowed guard holds this index's mutex.
 	void AssertHeld(const BoundIndex &index) const DUCKDB_ASSERT_CAPABILITY(this) DUCKDB_ASSERT_CAPABILITY(index.lock) {
 		D_ASSERT(&locked_index == &index);
+		(void)locked_index;
 	}
 
 private:
